 ## Background
-The concept was introduced by Teller et al., who required long preprocessing times and assumed axis-aligned cells [S1, unofficial]. Wonka et al. [152] presented a from-region visibility preprocessing algorithm with occluder fusion, limited to 2.5D datasets [S1, unofficial]. Durand et al. [41] extended this to 3D environments [S1, unofficial]. Chhugani et al. [20] developed a system focusing on image accuracy and levels of detail [S1, unofficial].
+The method was developed by Wonka et al. [152] and Durand et al. [41] [S1, unofficial]. Wonka et al. presented a from-region visibility preprocessing algorithm with occluder fusion [S1, unofficial]. Durand et al. presented a from-region visibility preprocessing algorithm that could handle 3D environments [S1, unofficial]. Chhugani et al. developed a system that precomputes from-region visibility and levels of detail per region [S1, unofficial].
 
